
## AI review loop (ai-review-kit — auto-run)

After opening ANY pull request in this repo, immediately and without being asked:

1. Fire the Codex review trigger: `gh pr comment <N> --body "@codex review"` (skip only
   if a Codex review/ack for this head already exists — e.g. the account's auto-review
   fired on PR open).
2. Drive the `pr-review-loop` skill (project-local, `.claude/skills/pr-review-loop/`) to
   convergence: triage → verified fixes → reply/resolve threads → re-trigger reviewers →
   repeat. It is autonomous by design; only its three escalation triggers stop for a
   human, and it NEVER merges.
3. Report the PR's end state in one line: converged (ready for human merge) or escalated
   (what and why). The human's job is the merge click.

Additionally — the babysitter: at the START of any session in this repo, check the
user's open PRs here for unhandled review findings, stale reviewer state, or a
converged-but-unannounced head (`gh search prs --author "@me" --state open`), and if
anything is actionable, run the pr-review-loop sweep unprompted before other work.
Cheap when idle: nothing actionable → say nothing and move on. (For coverage while no
session is open, each developer can once tell Claude Code: "schedule a recurring task:
babysit my PRs every 30 minutes".)

Installed by ai-review-kit's setup.sh — keep this section when editing CLAUDE.md.
